# This old man - traditioneel Engels telliedje, kinderlied
# Traditioneel, auteur onbekend (Roud 3550). Anne Gilchrist publiceerde in 1937 een versie
# die zij in de jaren 1870 van haar Welshe kindermeid had geleerd (Wikipedia (en)).
# Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit THIS_OLD.MAN (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). De bron noemt het refrein na het eerste
# couplet; het is na elk couplet met {chorus} herhaald.
{title: This old man}
{meta: id this-old-man}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit THIS_OLD.MAN (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via Wikipedia (en)}
{meta: tag kinderlied}
{meta: tag kampvuur}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played one,
He played nick nack on my drum
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
With a nick nack paddy wack
give a dog a bone
This old man came rolling home
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played two
He played nick nack on my shoe
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played three
He played nick nack on my knee
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played four
He played nick nack on my door
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played five
He played nick nack on my hive
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played six
He played nick nack on my sticks
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played seven
He played nick nack up to Devon
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played eight
He played nick nack on my pate
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played nine
He played nick nack on my spine
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
This old man, he played ten
He played nick nack on my hen.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
